  "full_task_complete": false,
  "full_goal_complete": false,
  "approved_work": "Reconcile accepted operations and external effects after crashes; mark interrupted live sessions honestly, query supported provider state and expose bounded operator reconciliation when certainty is unavailable. Prevent duplicate redial, stale bridge resurrection or database-only completion. Drain or terminate resources on shutdown.",
  "approved_verification": "Kill/restart around submit, answer, ready, commit and retirement. The recovered journal, provider state and actual media agree or explicitly report uncertainty; subsequent operations cannot bypass unresolved conflicting effects.",
  "initial_findings": [
    "Canonical startup obtains exclusive installation ownership, fences prior Connection observations, recovers operation work and installs actual native adapter absence recovery before intake.",
    "Graceful shutdown drains initialization, native peers, provider/telephone workers and record/HTTP listeners before installation retirement. These code paths alone do not prove abrupt process behavior.",
    "Earlier DTMF successor/restart cases and controlled Store recovery reports retain their narrower scopes. They are not relabeled as abrupt full operation recovery."
  ],
  "current_implementation": {
    "source": "crates/connect-server/tests/support/canonical_native_connections/crash_recovery.rs",
    "scope": "Actual subprocess native ready/committed decoded bridge and actual server answer before callback confirmation; parent SIGKILL, successor ownership, old physical readiness/lifetime fencing, honest failed unconfirmed offer, immutable replay/no duplicate admission, public snapshot and stale signal refusal. EdDSA and ES256. Actual submitted SIP call remains external after server SIGKILL: successor reports Unknown at original attempt1, clears readiness, preserves receipt, refuses operator-declared completion, and replay/conflicting invitation cause no redial. Store process-exit boundaries separately cover local transactions with a synthetic effect counter.",
    "entrypoint_policy": "One explicitly ignored child-only entry point is invoked by four parent tests using --ignored; never counted as a skipped qualification or standalone pass.",
    "verification": "Four native SIGKILL parents and two surviving-peer SIP SIGKILL parents pass, plus two Store parents/27 controlled process-exit boundaries. SIP constructor answer/end regressions pass. Every run retains source/executable guards; failed first SIP authorization fixture is retained separately."
  },
  "remaining": [
    "Qualify native retirement, SIP answered/ready/committed and retirement crash boundaries with still-live external peers; current six SIGKILL parent cases do not close the task.",
    "Qualify supported provider state queries after actual process death; prepared actual-SDK external-HTTP fixtures are building and are not yet qualification.",
    "Verify bounded authorized operator reconciliation for uncertainty and unresolved-conflict exclusion across required operation classes.",
    "Verify actual owned drain/termination, retained original consultation/handoff/replacement effects and recovery failure cases, then audit complete G6-047 coverage."
  ],
